 # MCP SDK
-# `rev` is REQUIRED, not decorative. Without it this dependency floats to the
-# default branch HEAD, and `cargo update` re-resolves straight past the
-# committed Cargo.lock — picking an rmcp whose `model::Content` no longer
-# exists (it is `ContentBlock` in 2.x). Reproduced 2026-07-31:
-# `rm Cargo.lock && cargo check` fails with E0432 + E0639, while a plain
-# `cargo check` succeeds on the stale lock. A lockfile records a resolution; it
-# does not constrain the next one.
-#
-# a64be231 is what the committed lockfile already resolves to, so pinning it
-# changes nothing today — it only stops the drift.
-rmcp = { git = "https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk", rev = "a64be231527f923e9f84d4dd7bf3c3bd695ee53e", features = [
+# Pinned to an EXACT registry version (`=3.4.0`), not a caret range. This
+# replaces a prior git `rev` pin (a64be231, rmcp 1.4.0) that existed to stop
+# `cargo update` from floating past the committed Cargo.lock onto a semver-
+# incompatible rmcp release. A registry version requirement has the same
+# floating risk with a caret (`^3.4.0` would happily take 3.5.0's breakage),
+# so the exact-version form (`=3.4.0`) is load-bearing here for the identical
+# reason the `rev` was: `model::Content` was renamed to `model::ContentBlock`,
+# `ServerInfo`/`ClientInfo` are now deprecated aliases for `ServerConfig`/
+# `ClientConfig`, and `ProgressNotificationParam` gained a required `meta`
+# field behind `#[non_exhaustive]` — each a compile break, not a warning.
+# Bumping this pin requires re-reading rmcp's CHANGELOG.md for the versions in
+# between and re-verifying the MCP protocol-version support matrix in
+# `tests/mcp_protocol_versions.rs`.
+rmcp = { version = "=3.4.0", features = [
     "server",
     "transport-io",
     "macros",
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index dcf8d15..d1c678c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@ SurrealDB storage, graph, vectors, events, task state
 
 The `crates/surreal-memory` library owns storage and embedding abstractions. The root binary supplies Axum REST/MCP routing, durable operation coordination, supervised execution, and background workers. Optional features include Memory Palace and CUDA/Metal acceleration.
 
+## MCP transports
+
+The MCP server (`src/mcp/`) is built on [rmcp](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk) `=3.4.0`, exposed over stdio (`MCP_STDIO=true`, the default) and streamable HTTP (mounted at `/mcp/http`, with legacy SSE compatibility routes at `/mcp/sse` and `/mcp/messages`). Both transports negotiate every MCP protocol revision the SDK knows: `2024-11-05`, `2025-03-26`, `2025-06-18`, `2025-11-25`, and `2026-07-28` (the last replaced the `initialize` handshake with `server/discover` plus per-request `_meta`, per SEP-2575). See `tests/mcp_protocol_versions.rs` for the version × transport coverage matrix.
+
 ## Build and test
 
 ```bash
diff --git a/docs/lessons.md b/docs/lessons.md
index b42e74e..7432e36 100644
--- a/docs/lessons.md
+++ b/docs/lessons.md
@@ -58,3 +58,11 @@ Format: `YYYY-MM-DD — Rule — *(context: what went wrong)*`
 - 2026-03-17 — One `cargo check` per change set. Do not re-run "to be sure."
 - 2026-03-17 — Test changes against the real consumer (UAR), not a toy test.
 - 2026-03-17 — For CLI/agent consumers, `user_id = "anonymous"` so scope filtering uses `agent_id`.
+
+## MCP / rmcp
+
+- 2026-09-25 — An MCP protocol-version support gap is a version-pin problem, not a code-logic problem: rmcp 1.4.0 predates 2025-11-25 support (added 1.5.0) and predates the 2026-07-28 discover/per-request-meta lifecycle (added 3.0.0-beta.1, SEP-2575). `ServerHandler::supported_protocol_versions` already defaults to `ProtocolVersion::KNOWN_VERSIONS` (every version the linked SDK knows) — the fix for "some clients can't initialize" was upgrading the dependency, not touching negotiation logic.
+- 2026-09-25 — `rmcp::model::Content` was renamed to `ContentBlock` and `ServerInfo`/`ClientInfo` became `#[deprecated]` aliases for `ServerConfig`/`ClientConfig` (same underlying `InitializeResult`/`InitializeRequestParams` type) between 1.4.0 and 3.4.0. `cargo clippy -D warnings` fails on the deprecated alias even though it still compiles — grep for the old names after any rmcp bump, don't rely on `cargo check` alone.
+- 2026-09-25 — `rmcp::model::ProgressNotificationParam` is `#[non_exhaustive]` and gained a required `meta` field in the same range; struct-literal construction from outside the crate stops compiling. Use the `::new(token, progress).with_message(..)` builder instead of assuming a plain struct literal survives a minor-looking SDK bump.
+- 2026-09-25 — When testing an MCP server's transport layer, drive it with hand-rolled raw JSON-RPC (newline-delimited over an in-process `tokio::io::duplex` for stdio; SSE-framed HTTP POSTs for streamable HTTP), not the SDK's own client. The real client population (Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.) does not link `rmcp`; a server that only satisfies its own SDK's client proves nothing about interop.
+- 2026-09-25 — The production `StreamableHttpServerConfig::default()` (`legacy_session_mode: true`, `json_response: false`) means even 2026-07-28's per-request-negotiated calls come back as `text/event-stream` SSE bodies on success, not plain JSON — a single SSE-aware response parser must be shared across every protocol version's HTTP test, not just the legacy ones.
